cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below, together with the paper."
title: "UDE-posets: code and data for 'Derived equivalences between diagram categories of finite posets'"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ascenzi
    given-names: Chiara
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6520-1975"
    affiliation: "Tampere University"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chiara-ascenzi/UDE-posets"
abstract: >-
  Python code and data for the paper "Derived equivalences between diagram
  categories of finite posets": admissible cuts of finite posets, the
  equivalence relation they generate on all posets with at most nine
  elements, its comparison with derived invariants, and the list of its
  classes on connected posets.
keywords:
  - finite posets
  - universal derived equivalence
  - incidence algebras
  - admissible cuts
  - Coxeter polynomial
